module lamd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }
import frcrimp.deadlines.{ SentencingScheduled }

// The Middle District of Louisiana's own criminal periods, counted under
// the criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). All
// criminal motions comply with Local Civil Rules 7, 10 and 11 (LCrR 12),
// so the civil rules' response period and memorandum page limits apply to
// them. No trigger carries a service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added
// days follow the manner of service, which is not modeled here.
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP periods stay in lit/frcrimp and are only named
// here: the presentence report's disclosure not less than thirty-five
// days before sentencing (LCrR 32(a)(2); FRCrimP 32(e)(2)), the written
// objections within fourteen days thereafter (LCrR 32(a)(2); FRCrimP
// 32(f)(1)), and the revised report and addendum not later than seven
// days before the sentencing hearing (LCrR 32(a)(4); FRCrimP 32(g)). The
// court may modify any LCrR 32 period for good cause, but the thirty-five
// day period may be diminished only with the defendant's consent (LCrR
// 32(a)(6)). A presentence report is deemed disclosed one day after a
// copy is filed electronically (LCrR 32(a)(8)); the corpus models no such
// deemed-disclosure trigger, so it stays in this note.
//
// A reply memorandum may be filed without leave only on a Rule 12 or Rule
// 56 motion of the civil rules, within fourteen days after service of the
// response (LR 7(f)); whether that reaches a criminal motion is not
// stated, so no criminal reply period is encoded. Conditions that are not
// deadlines from an event stay in notes: the pretrial services report is
// filed under seal before or immediately after the initial appearance
// (LCrR 5(b)); counsel and parties attend every stage of trial unless
// excused (LCrR 23); jurors are interviewed after trial only on leave of
// court for good cause (LCrR 24(b)); a motion to withdraw certifies that
// the client was notified of all deadlines (LCrR 44); the offering party
// keeps physical exhibits until any appeal is resolved or the time for
// appeal has expired (LCrR 55(e)(2)). Electronic filing and service (LCrR
// 49), extrajudicial statements (LCrR 53) and petty offenses (LCrR 58)
// state no period.
//
// The earlier M.D. La. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// (United States v. Salerno, Brady v. Maryland, Barker v. Wingo, Zedner v.
// United States, Boykin v. Alabama, Missouri v. Frye, Jackson v. Virginia,
// United States v. Booker, Roe v. Flores-Ortega, Garza v. Idaho) are
// FRCrimP, Speedy Trial Act or constitutional authority and belong to
// lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A memorandum supporting or opposing a criminal motion: at most
/// twenty-five pages excluding attachments, tables and the certificate of
/// service, unless leave is obtained (M.D. La. LCrR 12; LR 7(g)).
limit memorandum { pages <= 25 cite "M.D. La. LR 7(g)" } cite "M.D. La. LCrR 12; M.D. La. LR 7(g)"

/// A reply or surreply memorandum, if permitted: at most ten pages (M.D.
/// La. LCrR 12; LR 7(g)).
limit reply-memorandum {
  pages <= 10 cite "M.D. La. LR 7(g)"
} cite "M.D. La. LCrR 12; M.D. La. LR 7(g)"

/// A criminal motion is served (M.D. La. LCrR 12; LR 7(f)).
event MotionServed() paper memorandum
/// The case is finally disposed of (M.D. La. LCrR 55(f)).
event FinalDisposition()

/// M.D. La. LCrR 12; LR 7(f): each respondent opposing a motion files a
/// response, with opposing affidavits and supporting documents then
/// available, within twenty-one days after service of the motion; for
/// good cause the Court may order a shorter or longer period.
deadline response-period: 21.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "M.D. La. LCrR 12; M.D. La. LR 7(f)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// M.D. La. LCrR 32(b): a sentencing memorandum is filed under seal at
/// least fourteen days before the date of sentencing.
deadline sentencing-memorandum: 14.days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "M.D. La. LCrR 32(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// M.D. La. LCrR 32(c): a government motion under USSG § 5K1.1, with its
/// memorandum and a proposed order, is filed under seal at least fourteen
/// days before the date of sentencing.
deadline substantial-assistance-motion: 14.days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "M.D. La. LCrR 32(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// M.D. La. LCrR 55(f): exhibits in the Clerk's custody are removed by
/// the offering party within thirty days of the final disposition of the
/// case, failing which the Clerk may destroy or otherwise dispose of them.
deadline exhibit-removal: 30.days after FinalDisposition() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "M.D. La. LCrR 55(f)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
